wbemprox: Add proxies for the WMI interfaces.

Wine had no proxy/stub for IWbemServices, IEnumWbemClassObject,
IWbemCallResult and IWbemObjectSink, so none of them could be used from
another apartment (E_NOINTERFACE from RemQueryInterface). Generate them
from wbemcli.idl and register them under the proxy CLSID Windows uses.

The class objects, contexts and qualifier sets are local interfaces,
marshaled on Windows by fastprox's own IMarshal; aggregate the
free-threaded marshaler so that they pass through the proxies within the
process.

Affinity's installer asks WMI for Win32_Processor.Architecture from its
WPF thread; it got nothing, took that for an ARM64 machine, and warned
that the x64 installer is not recommended.
